 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property law, in relation to requiring residential\nleases to include information on prior flood damage",
    "basePrintNo": "S1335",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1335-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §231-b, RP L (as proposed in S.5472-A & A.7876-A)",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1335\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN-SIGAL\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property law, in relation to requiring residen-\ntial leases to include information on prior flood damage\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2022, ch.768, to modify a property\nowner's disclosure requirements related to prior flood damage.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation says that the lessor of a property must disclose to any\ntenants the existence and nature of any prior flood damage that the\nlessor knows or reasonably should know has occurred at the property. The\nchapter amendment does not affect separate disclosure requirements\nconcerning whether the property is in a specially designated flood zone.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 768 of the Laws of 2022. S.5472-A passed\nthe Senate in May 2022, and A.7876-A passed the Assembly in June 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the Laws of 2022 amending the real property law relating to\nrequiring disclosure of information concerning flood insurance on resi-\ndential leases, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.5472-A and\nA.7876-A, takes effect.\n",
